# ==============================================================================
# Redwood Retail: Environment Configuration Template
# Copy this file to .env and configure values for your Google Cloud environment.
# deploy.sh sources the .env and maps it onto the Terraform TF_VAR_* inputs, so
# the names below are the names something actually reads.
# ==============================================================================

# Google Cloud Platform Settings
GCP_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project-id
GCP_REGION=europe-west4

# Firestore Enterprise Settings (Native Mode)
FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID=redwood
FIRESTORE_COLLECTION=retail
# Customer profiles, replicated to BigQuery alongside the orders and read by the
# loyalty agent. deploy.sh, the CDC service and the seeder each default this to
# "customers"; set it here if you want it to be anything else.
FIRESTORE_CUSTOMERS_COLLECTION=customers

# Optional. Where the bridge, the agent and the CDC service write the latency
# spans the console's pipeline panel renders. No Eventarc trigger watches this
# collection, so writing to it cannot feed back into the pipeline it measures.
# FIRESTORE_TRACES_COLLECTION=pipeline_traces

# Optional. Only orders whose document id starts with this are traced, which in
# practice means orders placed from the app. Tracing everything would write a
# record for each of the 400 seeded documents during a backfill and bury the
# order the presenter just placed. Set empty to disable order tracing.
# TRACE_DOCUMENT_ID_PREFIX=ORD-26-MOB-

# BigQuery Data Warehouse & BQML
BIGQUERY_DATASET=redwood_retail
# The append-only ledger. This said orders_cdc while .env, the Terraform default
# and every query and document said retail_cdc, so an environment built from
# this template streamed its changes into a table nothing else read.
BIGQUERY_CDC_TABLE=retail_cdc
BIGQUERY_HISTORICAL_VIEW=customer_historical_data
BIGQUERY_CHURN_MODEL=customer_churn_model

# Optional. Typed mirror of live order state, created by Terraform as
# <FIRESTORE_COLLECTION>_current. deploy.sh and the churn function derive it
# from FIRESTORE_COLLECTION, so only set it if you renamed the table.
# BIGQUERY_ORDERS_TABLE=retail_current

# Optional. Batch churn scores read by the loyalty agent and the mobile backend.
# BIGQUERY_PREDICTIONS_TABLE=customer_churn_risk

# Cloud Storage & pipeline identity
GCS_BUCKET_PREFIX=redwood-retail
# Replication is Eventarc -> Cloud Run -> BigQuery Storage Write API; there is no
# Dataflow job anywhere in this deployment. Only the service account id still
# carries the Dataflow name, and it stays: renaming it would make Terraform
# destroy and recreate the account and drop every IAM grant on it, purely
# cosmetically. deploy.sh accepts PIPELINE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT as an alias.
DATAFLOW_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=dataflow-redwood-sa

# Optional. Who may open the app and console. Neither redwood-app nor
# redwood-churn allows unauthenticated access, so reaching them means holding
# roles/run.invoker and going through `gcloud run services proxy`.
#
# deploy.sh grants this to whoever runs it, which is why a solo deployment
# needs nothing here. Set it to hand access to colleagues as well; it replaces
# the default rather than adding to it, so include yourself.
# Comma-separated, each entry a fully qualified IAM member.
# APP_INVOKER_MEMBERS=user:you@example.com,user:colleague@example.com

# Optional. Artifact Registry repository holding the service images.
# ARTIFACT_REPOSITORY=pipeline-images

# Optional. Agent Engine deployment (scripts/deploy_agent_engine.py). The bridge
# resolves the agent by display name, so this must match agent_display_name in
# terraform/agent_bridge.tf if you change it.
# AGENT_DISPLAY_NAME=redwood-loyalty-agent
# REASONING_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Optional. Which BigQuery churn tiers may be escalated by the LLM judge.
#
# The judge is only consulted when the model's tier is in this list AND the
# customer has filed a complaint after the score was calculated -- a complaint
# the overnight model provably cannot have seen. Anything already at HIGH or
# CRITICAL qualifies on the model's own number and never needs a judgement.
#
# LOW is included so the demo1 beat works: a healthy customer files a one-star
# review, and the agent has to reason about whether that changes the picture.
# Narrow this to MODERATE to make escalation rarer in production, at the cost
# of that beat.
# ESCALATION_CANDIDATE_TIERS=MODERATE,LOW
